# Line-ending policy.
#
# The CI release gate regenerates the artifacts below and then requires
# `git status --porcelain` to be empty. That comparison is only meaningful if the
# checkout form of these files is deterministic: without a rule here it depends on
# the runner's `core.autocrlf`, and a runner configured with autocrlf=false would
# fail the gate even though the generated content is correct.
#
# `.gitattributes` takes precedence over `core.autocrlf`, so `eol=lf` pins the
# checkout form on every platform. The committed blobs are already LF, so this
# changes no stored content and requires no renormalization.
#
# Keep this list in sync with scripts/generate_artifacts.py.
VERSION.json             text eol=lf
docs/REGISTRY-SUMMARY.md text eol=lf
docs/INDEX.html          text eol=lf
